  "conclusion": "On Logic in es-ES, the four track-header checkboxes were found by the descriptions isMuted by 'Silenciar', isSoloed by 'Solo', isArmed by 'Activar grabación', isInputMonitoring by 'Monitorización de entrada', each the value of Apple's row this record cites. In the readings where logic://tracks served rows a header read wrote (A_all_on, B_solo_released, C_all_off), 23 of the 24 cells whose checkbox read 0 or 1 were published as that value. 1 published cell disagrees with the checkbox, listed in the tally. It is the Mute of a track the solo silenced, published true while its checkbox read 0, and in that read the rows published muted are exactly the first MCU bank's strips other than the soloed track (rows_published_muted): the value is the MCU Mute LED that lights on a strip a solo silences, not a header read. Verdict partial by the rule in the tally.",
  "limits": [
    "One host and one disposable project (the 19-track locale-campaign fixture); track 2 carries the toggles and track 3 is the one read off. Other builds, other track types and a hidden or collapsed header are not measured.",
    "Logic draws a soloed track's own Mute checkbox as 0, so no single reading shows all four on: reading A has Solo, Record Enable and Input Monitoring on, reading B has Mute, Record Enable and Input Monitoring on.",
    "While a track is soloed, the Mute checkbox of every track the solo silences read -1 in some walks and 0 in others; the product publishes a -1 as unread and a 0 as false, and which one a read meets depends on when it lands. Those cells are counted apart, not compared.",
    "A logic://tracks read is compared with the header walk taken right after it, not at the same instant; the walk before the read is recorded, and ax_same_before_and_after_the_read says whether the header moved in between.",
    "system.refresh_cache answered refreshed: true in reads that still served the rows MCU feedback creates (no fetched_at, eight rows); why the header read did not replace them is not measured here.",
    "Input Monitoring was set and cleared by the harness (AXFocused, then AXPress on the checkbox), not by the product, which has no Input Monitoring write."
  ],
  "supersedes": null
}
